00:42:01.871 --> 00:42:03.177
What?


00:42:03.307 --> 00:42:05.657
The phone went dead.


00:42:05.789 --> 00:42:07.007
That's strange.


00:42:20.543 --> 00:42:21.760
Are all the lines down?


00:42:24.023 --> 00:42:25.023
I'm not sure.


00:42:27.811 --> 00:42:29.681
Is your mom around?


00:42:29.813 --> 00:42:30.813
Should be.


00:42:34.164 --> 00:42:35.208
Mom, you here?


00:42:36.297 --> 00:42:37.297
Mom!


00:42:37.429 --> 00:42:38.429
Georgia?


00:42:45.697 --> 00:42:47.873
This one's dead, too.


00:42:48.005 --> 00:42:50.268
- Hey, boys.
- Jesus, Joseph, and Mary.


00:42:53.313 --> 00:42:55.925
She got you, Bobby.


00:42:57.362 --> 00:42:58.818
I've been scaring the
socks off that kid


00:42:58.842 --> 00:43:00.190
since he was two.


00:43:00.320 --> 00:43:02.125
Hey, well, it's not funny
you gave me a heart attack.


00:43:02.148 --> 00:43:03.715
What's going on?


00:43:03.847 --> 00:43:05.021
The phones are dead.


00:43:05.152 --> 00:43:06.197
Yeah.


00:43:06.327 --> 00:43:07.893
All of 'em?


00:43:08.025 --> 00:43:09.242
Every single one of 'em.


00:43:12.333 --> 00:43:13.333
Georgia, what is it?


00:43:15.032 --> 00:43:16.313
The sheriff was in
here this morning


00:43:16.336 --> 00:43:18.512
and he was concerned
about something,


00:43:18.643 --> 00:43:21.211
but I couldn't put my
finger on it.


00:43:23.126 --> 00:43:25.737
It could just be a
technical thing.


00:43:25.869 --> 00:43:27.827
No need to work ourselves
silly about it, right?


00:43:27.958 --> 00:43:29.757
Well, sure, Bobby,
but we just saw the sheriff


00:43:29.873 --> 00:43:32.353
squeal outta here like a
bat outta hell.


00:43:39.012 --> 00:43:41.797
Here off the 112 headed
to Bill Unger's property.


00:43:41.927 --> 00:43:42.668
Copy that, Liz.


00:43:42.798 --> 00:43:44.235
Everything okay?


00:43:44.364 --> 00:43:45.757
Not sure.


00:43:45.889 --> 00:43:48.282
What'd you find out
about the dog?


00:43:48.413 --> 00:43:49.956
You know, I'm not
sure I wanna discuss that


00:43:49.980 --> 00:43:51.721
till we're back at the office.


00:43:51.851 --> 00:43:53.371
I'm pulling into town in
a few seconds,


00:43:53.460 --> 00:43:55.420
so I'll see you both
when you get back, okay?


00:43:57.378 --> 00:43:59.206
Copy that, Teddy.


00:43:59.336 --> 00:44:00.599
All right, Teddy out.


00:44:02.862 --> 00:44:04.210
Well, he's here right now.


00:44:24.231 --> 00:44:25.623
Hey, what are y'all doing here?


00:44:25.755 --> 00:44:26.972
You okay, Teddy?


00:44:27.103 --> 00:44:29.672
Yeah, tell us
what's going on, Teddy.


00:44:29.802 --> 00:44:31.804
Uh, I'm not really sure I
can explain it right now.


00:44:31.934 --> 00:44:33.284
Do the best you can, son.


00:44:35.155 --> 00:44:36.155
Okay, Rick.


00:44:36.286 --> 00:44:38.376
Well, I went out looking
for Bernard's dog,


00:44:38.505 --> 00:44:42.119
I didn't find it, but I came
across Timmy's bike and...


00:44:42.248 --> 00:44:43.248
And what?


00:44:47.166 --> 00:44:51.128
Yeah, I don't know, look,
I need to make a phone call.


00:44:51.257 --> 00:44:52.128
I need to call Timmy's parents


00:44:52.259 --> 00:44:53.280
and make sure he got home safe.


00:44:53.304 --> 00:44:55.045
Rick says all the phone
lines are down.


00:44:56.393 --> 00:44:57.221
All of 'em?


00:44:57.351 --> 00:44:58.351
All of 'em.


00:45:01.920 --> 00:45:03.096
I've seen that look before.


00:45:04.184 --> 00:45:05.445
Bill.


00:45:05.577 --> 00:45:06.795
Unger?


00:45:06.925 --> 00:45:07.925
Yeah.


00:45:08.014 --> 00:45:09.121
Yeah, he was in town this
morning spouting


00:45:09.146 --> 00:45:11.322
his usual crazy nonsense.


00:45:11.452 --> 00:45:13.367
This time something about
people on his property


00:45:13.498 --> 00:45:15.282
doing some weird stuff.


00:45:15.413 --> 00:45:17.588
Weird stuff?


00:45:17.719 --> 00:45:19.393
Yeah, he said to look
out for the phone lines.


00:45:19.416 --> 00:45:20.766
What does that mean?


00:45:20.896 --> 00:45:21.724
Uh, the phone lines.


00:45:21.853 --> 00:45:23.550
He said...


00:45:23.681 --> 00:45:25.684
He was going on about
communications.


00:45:25.815 --> 00:45:28.731
Teddy, where are the sheriff
and Liz headed to now?


00:45:31.297 --> 00:45:32.297
Bill's place.


00:46:38.235 --> 00:46:39.235
That looks like blood.


00:46:42.586 --> 00:46:43.717
Yes, it does.


00:47:01.387 --> 00:47:02.387
What is that?


00:47:08.481 --> 00:47:09.481
He mine the place?


00:47:10.744 --> 00:47:12.443
It would appear that way now,
wouldn't it?


00:47:15.445 --> 00:47:16.577
Where's Bill?


00:47:18.405 --> 00:47:19.492
I don't know.


00:47:32.463 --> 00:47:33.507
Sheriff?


00:47:35.378 --> 00:47:37.032
Sheriff?


00:47:37.163 --> 00:47:38.163
Give me a second.


00:47:40.340 --> 00:47:41.340
Joe!


00:49:11.083 --> 00:49:12.083
This is Teddy for Joe.


00:49:12.170 --> 00:49:13.215
Come in, Joe.


00:49:16.045 --> 00:49:17.436
Liz, do you read me?


00:49:20.092 --> 00:49:21.702
Liz, give me a read here.
Anything.


00:49:23.878 --> 00:49:25.619
Maybe they're talking to Bill.


00:49:25.750 --> 00:49:28.012
Sure, maybe they aren't
by their radio.


00:49:28.143 --> 00:49:29.927
No.


00:49:30.059 --> 00:49:33.452
No, a big city cop we're
talking about here.


00:49:33.583 --> 00:49:35.585
He ain't dumb.


00:49:35.715 --> 00:49:38.023
He done do things the
way we do here.


00:49:38.153 --> 00:49:39.329
What's that supposed to mean?


00:49:39.458 --> 00:49:41.373
He just means Joe's a
skeptical guy, that's all.


00:49:41.505 --> 00:49:43.159
I can clarify that.


00:49:43.289 --> 00:49:44.608
Even with Bill's
crazy ass stories


00:49:44.681 --> 00:49:45.987
he still wanted to investigate.


00:49:47.902 --> 00:49:49.228
I guess it takes somebody
from out of town


00:49:49.251 --> 00:49:51.731
to think that guy's not
totally off his nut.


00:49:51.862 --> 00:49:53.342
I wonder if Timmy's
folks have a CB.


00:49:54.909 --> 00:49:57.128
All right, so what do we do?


00:49:57.260 --> 00:49:59.217
Why the hell you
looking at me for?


00:49:59.349 --> 00:50:00.891
There's your new leader
of the pack right there.


00:50:00.914 --> 00:50:02.307
No, no.


00:50:02.438 --> 00:50:04.005
Joe will be back.


00:50:04.135 --> 00:50:05.963
All right, he'll be back.
We just stay put.


00:50:06.094 --> 00:50:08.748
And what do we do if he
don't come back?


00:50:08.880 --> 00:50:09.880
All right.


00:50:11.403 --> 00:50:13.318
I'm gonna drive my rig
over to Bill's,


00:50:14.451 --> 00:50:15.887
see what I can drum up.


00:50:17.889 --> 00:50:20.282
I'll stay on the short
wave and listen


00:50:20.413 --> 00:50:22.675
for anything that comes in.


00:50:22.806 --> 00:50:24.547
All right, I guess I'll
make the rounds


00:50:24.677 --> 00:50:26.221
and make sure that
everybody's staying calm.


00:50:26.244 --> 00:50:27.701
And I guess I better
go make sure Bernard's


00:50:27.724 --> 00:50:29.726
not out looking for
his goddamn dog.


00:50:29.856 --> 00:50:32.137
Just stay calm, I'll go over
and check on Harry and Deanna


00:50:32.164 --> 00:50:34.557
and I'll fill them in
on the situation, Teddy.


00:50:34.688 --> 00:50:35.688
All right, Bobby.


00:50:50.574 --> 00:50:52.445
Hey, Rick.


00:50:52.576 --> 00:50:53.793
I thought you were leaving.


00:50:54.882 --> 00:50:56.753
Look, I got a problem.


00:50:56.884 --> 00:50:59.409
- Somebody ran off with my...
- Somebody lifted my battery.


00:51:04.762 --> 00:51:06.458
How much you wanna bet
every other vehicle


00:51:06.590 --> 00:51:08.722
on this block is inoperable?


00:51:10.637 --> 00:51:11.811
Bet you $5.


00:51:24.563 --> 00:51:26.043
Someone don't want us leavin'.


00:51:41.233 --> 00:51:43.670
Um, hello?


00:51:46.498 --> 00:51:48.389
Though I could pretty much
guarantee that I got nothing


00:51:48.414 --> 00:51:50.721
in the shop that's gonna
fit in that cruiser.


00:51:50.851 --> 00:51:52.461
But if the lines are
back up I can give


00:51:52.592 --> 00:51:53.952
a call into Ingram
tomorrow morning


00:51:53.985 --> 00:51:55.507
and that's the best I
can do for you.


00:51:55.639 --> 00:51:57.335
I appreciate it, Rick.


00:51:57.467 --> 00:51:59.139
I've seen enough weird
shit in the last 24 hours,


00:51:59.164 --> 00:52:00.764
I don't wanna wait till
tomorrow morning.


00:52:01.688 --> 00:52:03.168
Okay.


00:52:03.298 --> 00:52:04.623
You have somewhere
secure to hole up?


00:52:04.648 --> 00:52:05.648
I'm right here.


00:52:06.518 --> 00:52:07.518
All right.


00:52:09.304 --> 00:52:10.304
What do you want?


00:52:16.485 --> 00:52:17.485
Harry!


00:52:18.356 --> 00:52:19.880
Teddy!


00:52:20.010 --> 00:52:21.490
Someone!


00:52:21.621 --> 00:52:22.621
Help!


00:52:24.581 --> 00:52:26.364
Rick, you stay here.


00:52:36.766 --> 00:52:38.724
Harry! Teddy!


00:52:38.856 --> 00:52:39.856
Teddy!


00:52:39.943 --> 00:52:41.336
Somebody help!


00:52:48.822 --> 00:52:50.302
Where's the other one?


00:52:50.432 --> 00:52:51.476
What other one?


00:53:03.402 --> 00:53:04.402
Come on.


00:53:12.018 --> 00:53:13.282
Die!


00:53:22.681 --> 00:53:24.117
All right, you stay put, Bobby.


00:53:24.248 --> 00:53:25.597
Okay, you guys.


00:53:25.728 --> 00:53:26.860
I want you to get inside!


00:53:29.559 --> 00:53:31.690
All right, come on you
sons of bitches.


00:53:31.822 --> 00:53:32.692
Close the door!


00:53:32.822 --> 00:53:34.041
Harry, no, come on.


00:53:34.172 --> 00:53:35.869
- No, no, no, no.
- Come on.


00:53:36.000 --> 00:53:38.219
Shut the goddamn door!


00:53:38.349 --> 00:53:40.047
Harry!


00:54:20.304 --> 00:54:21.567
Show yourselves!


00:54:25.266 --> 00:54:26.266
Come on!


00:54:32.056 --> 00:54:34.797
I ain't in the mood for
no hide and seek.


00:55:06.786 --> 00:55:08.918
What's with all the gunshots?


00:55:09.048 --> 00:55:11.313
I'm not so sure I know
what's going on.


00:55:14.664 --> 00:55:15.925
It's better we stay here.


00:55:19.277 --> 00:55:20.844
Gunshots from Rick's place.


00:55:22.715 --> 00:55:23.715
Can you see him?


00:55:25.282 --> 00:55:27.851
No, but Rick's a smart fella.


00:55:27.981 --> 00:55:29.219
Yeah, well smarts don't
matter if they get


00:55:29.242 --> 00:55:31.070
the jump on you like
these fellas have.


00:55:31.202 --> 00:55:32.202
We've seen that.


00:55:33.682 --> 00:55:35.003
How the hell do they
move so fast?


00:55:35.119 --> 00:55:36.119
Who are these people?


00:55:37.817 --> 00:55:38.817
I don't know.


00:55:41.255 --> 00:55:43.300
We have any guns in here?


00:55:43.431 --> 00:55:44.954
No.


00:55:45.085 --> 00:55:46.782
Harry's always hated the
damned things.


00:55:48.132 --> 00:55:49.306
Yeah.


00:56:23.601 --> 00:56:25.125
All right.


00:56:25.255 --> 00:56:26.474
Wanna dance?


00:56:29.695 --> 00:56:30.695
Let's tango.


00:56:37.920 --> 00:56:39.400
Son of a bitch.


00:56:41.402 --> 00:56:43.317
How many of you
fuckers are there?


00:56:53.197 --> 00:56:54.416
See ya, kitties.


00:56:59.898 --> 00:57:00.900
Shit.


00:57:03.989 --> 00:57:05.034
Holy shit.


00:57:06.210 --> 00:57:08.603
Oh, my God.


00:57:08.733 --> 00:57:10.431
All right, I gotta get
back to the station.


00:57:11.693 --> 00:57:12.869
You can't go out there.


00:57:12.998 --> 00:57:14.565
Yeah, she's right, Teddy,
you can't.


00:57:14.697 --> 00:57:16.088
No, there's no other option.


00:57:17.612 --> 00:57:18.612
Why?


00:57:19.963 --> 00:57:22.226
I got another revolver
in the office,


00:57:22.356 --> 00:57:24.750
ammo, and I'm pretty sure
I have a shotgun


00:57:24.880 --> 00:57:25.969
in the back of the cruiser.


00:57:27.318 --> 00:57:29.451
Shit, it might be in
Joe's cruiser.


00:57:29.581 --> 00:57:31.103
Come on. Think, Teddy, think.


00:57:33.846 --> 00:57:34.717
Teddy.


00:57:34.847 --> 00:57:35.847
Here.


00:57:36.980 --> 00:57:38.110
Take that.


00:57:38.242 --> 00:57:40.244
My god, what is this
thing doing in here?


00:57:40.373 --> 00:57:41.612
Harry always made us
keep it in case


00:57:41.637 --> 00:57:43.159
anybody ever tried to
rob the place.


00:57:47.164 --> 00:57:48.773
Yeah, right.


00:57:48.905 --> 00:57:49.992
Yeah, as if.


00:57:50.994 --> 00:57:52.822
Okay.


00:57:52.952 --> 00:57:55.867
It's only about 100 feet
to the station, all right?


00:57:55.998 --> 00:57:57.358
As soon as I get in
there I can try


00:57:57.434 --> 00:57:59.436
and hail somebody on
the short wave.


00:57:59.568 --> 00:58:01.047
Hang in there, okay?


00:58:01.177 --> 00:58:02.527
All right.


00:58:02.657 --> 00:58:04.458
Hey, y'all, there's
something moving in there.


00:58:08.141 --> 00:58:09.141
What the hell?


00:58:09.228 --> 00:58:11.188
Is that one of us?


00:58:11.318 --> 00:58:12.581
I think it's Rick.


00:58:12.710 --> 00:58:14.452
Yeah.


00:58:27.552 --> 00:58:29.032
Bernard!


00:58:33.905 --> 00:58:35.820
Bernard?


00:58:35.952 --> 00:58:36.952
Bernard!


00:59:05.851 --> 00:59:06.983
What happened?


00:59:32.094 --> 00:59:33.704
Come on, come on.


00:59:37.490 --> 00:59:38.579
- Hurry, come on.
- Come on.


00:59:38.710 --> 00:59:39.710
Come on.


00:59:45.891 --> 00:59:47.110
Where's Rick?


00:59:48.677 --> 00:59:49.677
He didn't make it.


00:59:51.722 --> 00:59:54.072
We watched him go into
Bernard's and...


00:59:56.335 --> 00:59:57.336
Oh, my God.


00:59:59.818 --> 01:00:02.125
What is going on?


01:00:02.255 --> 01:00:04.954
Georgia, have you been
keeping an ear on the radio?


01:00:05.083 --> 01:00:07.043
Yeah, but there's nothing.


01:00:07.172 --> 01:00:07.956
Nothing?


01:00:08.086 --> 01:00:09.086
Nothing.


01:00:09.132 --> 01:00:10.523
Nothing from Joe or Liz?


01:00:10.655 --> 01:00:11.655
Nothing.


01:00:13.135 --> 01:00:15.659
Mom, do you think we
can call out?


01:00:15.791 --> 01:00:18.315
Best we could do is
broadcast out


01:00:18.445 --> 01:00:21.884
and hope somebody driving
by has their radio on.


01:00:22.014 --> 01:00:23.581
Yeah, that's a hell
of a long shot.


01:00:26.844 --> 01:00:27.844
But it could work.


01:00:29.804 --> 01:00:31.588
You got any more
shells for that?


01:00:31.719 --> 01:00:33.983
The two shells I just
spent have been sitting


01:00:34.112 --> 01:00:35.724
in this thing for seven years.


01:00:35.853 --> 01:00:38.900
Why the fuck would I have
any more shells?


01:00:39.030 --> 01:00:40.467
Okay, Georgia.


01:00:40.597 --> 01:00:42.905
Well, I have more shells but
they're back at the station.


01:00:43.034 --> 01:00:44.034
Yeah.


01:00:44.123 --> 01:00:45.994
Mom, you got here
with no problem,


01:00:46.125 --> 01:00:48.650
so maybe Teddy can get back
down a few doors without issue.


01:00:48.780 --> 01:00:50.302
How many of them are there?


01:00:52.478 --> 01:00:53.871
We don't even know, do we?


01:00:56.353 --> 01:00:58.050
Do we even know what they want?


01:01:03.664 --> 01:01:05.014
There was something else.


01:01:08.320 --> 01:01:09.452
What do you mean, Cindy?


01:01:11.237 --> 01:01:13.586
There is something in
those trees.


01:01:15.240 --> 01:01:16.764
It got Rick.


01:01:18.592 --> 01:01:20.943
What like another one
of those people?


01:01:21.072 --> 01:01:22.072
No, no.


01:01:22.161 --> 01:01:24.250
It was like something inhuman.


01:01:38.742 --> 01:01:40.353
I'm gonna have to go
to the station.


01:01:41.440 --> 01:01:42.833
Teddy, you can't.


01:01:42.965 --> 01:01:43.965
It's okay, Deanna.


01:01:45.010 --> 01:01:46.010
It's my job.


01:01:47.969 --> 01:01:51.103
All right, y'all are
gonna have to stay here.


01:01:51.233 --> 01:01:52.452
Hold this place down.


01:01:52.583 --> 01:01:53.603
As soon as I leave you lock


01:01:53.626 --> 01:01:54.778
this place up, you understand,
Bobby?


01:01:54.802 --> 01:01:55.802
All right.


01:01:57.849 --> 01:01:59.721
Deanna, you still
have that radio?


01:02:09.034 --> 01:02:10.121
Yeah, okay.


01:02:10.253 --> 01:02:12.342
All right, I can use this
to call you guys


01:02:12.472 --> 01:02:14.431
from the station but you
won't be able to respond.


01:02:15.606 --> 01:02:17.260
Take this.


01:02:17.389 --> 01:02:19.565
Do you a lot more good than us.


01:02:19.697 --> 01:02:20.717
Georgia, what the hell
am I gonna do


01:02:20.742 --> 01:02:22.047
with an empty shotgun?


01:02:24.222 --> 01:02:26.704
Look, I got another
pistol in the office.


01:02:26.835 --> 01:02:28.923
I'll get you some more
shells for that


01:02:29.054 --> 01:02:30.534
and then I'll hustle back here.


01:02:30.664 --> 01:02:32.231
And then what?


01:02:32.362 --> 01:02:33.623
As soon as the sun comes up


01:02:35.452 --> 01:02:37.322
I will walk us outta
here if I have to.


01:02:42.327 --> 01:02:43.329
Okay.


01:02:44.590 --> 01:02:45.766
What are they doing?


01:02:53.425 --> 01:02:55.210
What are they doing?


01:02:55.340 --> 01:02:56.342
What the hell?


01:03:02.217 --> 01:03:03.958
They're feeding
whatever's in there.


01:03:12.880 --> 01:03:14.601
I'm not so sure going
out there is the best.


01:03:20.713 --> 01:03:22.873
Must've gone out back, I'm
gonna make sure it's locked.


01:03:47.958 --> 01:03:48.958
Come on.


01:03:49.003 --> 01:03:50.005
Okay.


01:04:19.295 --> 01:04:20.862
Come on. Come on.


01:04:31.262 --> 01:04:36.007
Get the hell inside now!


01:04:41.317 --> 01:04:42.840
Come on, come on!


01:04:51.195 --> 01:04:52.719
Jesus Christ!


01:04:52.849 --> 01:04:53.938
Joe, you're alive!


01:04:54.068 --> 01:04:55.068
Oh yeah.


01:04:56.114 --> 01:04:58.333
Here.


01:04:58.463 --> 01:05:00.422
Anybody comes through
that door, you kill it.


01:05:03.338 --> 01:05:04.382
Where's Liz?


01:05:11.389 --> 01:05:13.262
What the hell's going on here,
Joe?


01:05:13.391 --> 01:05:14.697
Oh, haven't you heard?


01:05:14.827 --> 01:05:16.148
Some asshole said
some fancy words


01:05:16.264 --> 01:05:18.266
and raised a goddamn
demon outta hell.


01:05:22.880 --> 01:05:24.054
What the hell do they want?


01:05:25.534 --> 01:05:26.534
Ain't it obvious?


01:05:32.280 --> 01:05:34.195
We saw them feeding it.


01:05:34.326 --> 01:05:35.675
There you go.


01:05:35.806 --> 01:05:38.112
Serving us up like dinner
on a goddamn silver platter.


01:05:38.242 --> 01:05:39.242
Shit.


01:05:41.159 --> 01:05:43.335
They're even feeding
it their dead.


01:05:51.213 --> 01:05:52.518
You saw it, didn't you, Joe?


01:05:54.737 --> 01:05:56.434
Up close and personal.


01:05:57.653 --> 01:05:58.871
How'd you get away from it?


01:06:01.788 --> 01:06:05.530
I wined it, dined it,
and then I claymore mined it.


01:06:07.010 --> 01:06:08.577
Where were you?


01:06:08.708 --> 01:06:11.842
Bill's front yard.


01:06:11.972 --> 01:06:13.061
Joe.


01:06:14.452 --> 01:06:15.715
Look in the evidence locker.


01:06:26.465 --> 01:06:27.465
Holy shit.


01:06:29.380 --> 01:06:30.773
Where the hell did you get this?


01:06:30.903 --> 01:06:32.317
We caught Bill using
it a couple years back


01:06:32.340 --> 01:06:34.125
trying to get rid of a
mole problem.


01:06:34.255 --> 01:06:36.822
The sheriff before, he had
to wrestle it away from him.


01:06:36.954 --> 01:06:38.302
Thank you, Bill.


01:06:40.523 --> 01:06:41.914
Where the hell are these guys?


01:06:44.570 --> 01:06:45.918
Who's left?


01:06:46.050 --> 01:06:48.487
We've got Cindy, Georgia,
Bobby and Deanna


01:06:48.617 --> 01:06:49.793
all locked in at the grille.


01:06:51.054 --> 01:06:52.925
All right.


01:06:53.056 --> 01:06:54.512
You gotta make sure that
they stay alive,


01:06:54.536 --> 01:06:55.407
and when the time is right,


01:06:55.538 --> 01:06:57.235
you're gonna get
them outta town.


01:06:57.365 --> 01:06:59.019
How am I gonna do that?


01:06:59.150 --> 01:07:01.630
Oh, we're gonna level the
playing field.


01:07:01.760 --> 01:07:04.199
Where they feeding him at?


01:07:04.329 --> 01:07:05.914
Uh, last we saw it was over
at Bernard's tree farm,


01:07:05.938 --> 01:07:08.072
but shit, it could be
anywhere by now.


01:07:10.987 --> 01:07:12.617
Rick told me you were
a good football player.


01:07:12.641 --> 01:07:13.773
Is that true?


01:07:13.903 --> 01:07:15.688
I was back in high school, why?


01:07:17.385 --> 01:07:19.039
I want you to run
straight up the middle,


01:07:19.170 --> 01:07:21.041
draw as many of those
Michael Myers wannabes


01:07:21.172 --> 01:07:22.172
with you as you can.


01:07:23.434 --> 01:07:24.434
Okay.


01:07:25.568 --> 01:07:26.786
Who's Michael Myers?


01:07:29.876 --> 01:07:32.356
Oh, for Christ's sakes
just holster this thing up.


01:07:33.576 --> 01:07:34.706
What are you gonna do?


01:07:37.362 --> 01:07:40.757
Oh, I have a date with a
big toothy horny monster


01:07:40.887 --> 01:07:42.498
and it's about to get fucked!


01:07:44.021 --> 01:07:45.762
Okay, okay.


01:07:49.896 --> 01:07:50.896
Georgia.


01:07:55.554 --> 01:07:57.990
I'm over at the sheriff's
station and Joe's here,


01:07:58.121 --> 01:08:00.690
he's, he's alive.


01:08:00.820 --> 01:08:02.648
I'm on the way back to you,
Georgia.


01:08:02.778 --> 01:08:04.519
God, I hope you can hear this.


01:08:04.650 --> 01:08:06.289
You better be ready to get
that door open.


01:08:16.096 --> 01:08:17.096
Mom, Mom.


01:08:17.140 --> 01:08:19.011
Bobby, no!


01:08:24.713 --> 01:08:26.106
Oh, my God.


01:08:28.109 --> 01:08:29.849
Go get some towels!


01:08:29.979 --> 01:08:32.417
- Bobby, Bobby.
- Here, here, here.


01:08:32.547 --> 01:08:35.854
How did he stab him?


01:08:35.985 --> 01:08:38.728
Bobby, Bobby, Bobby, Bobby,
look at me.


01:08:38.858 --> 01:08:40.599
Duct tape or any other
kind of tape.


01:08:40.729 --> 01:08:41.992
I don't see any.


01:08:43.211 --> 01:08:44.515
Breathe, Bobby.


01:08:44.646 --> 01:08:45.908
Breathe, breathe.


01:08:46.038 --> 01:08:47.127
Breathe, Bobby.


01:08:47.257 --> 01:08:49.346
- Bobby, look at me.
- Really tight.


01:08:49.478 --> 01:08:51.479
It's gonna be
okay. You'll be okay.


01:08:51.609 --> 01:08:54.177
- I'm sorry, I'm sorry.
- No, no, no, no, no.


01:08:54.309 --> 01:08:55.832
Don't say that, don't say that.


01:08:55.962 --> 01:08:57.615
There's nothing to be sorry for.


01:08:57.747 --> 01:08:59.748
Bobby, Bobby, Bobby, Bobby.


01:09:01.881 --> 01:09:03.622
It's okay, it's okay.


01:09:03.752 --> 01:09:04.753
Just breathe son.


01:09:04.884 --> 01:09:06.189
Deanna, put some
pressure on him.


01:09:06.320 --> 01:09:07.452
Bobby, stay with me.


01:09:07.582 --> 01:09:09.323
Look at me, look at me.


01:09:09.453 --> 01:09:10.453
Look at me.


01:09:13.676 --> 01:09:14.676
Bobby.


01:09:18.028 --> 01:09:20.856
It's all right,
you're gonna be okay.


01:09:20.987 --> 01:09:23.947
Bobby, Bobby, come back to me.


01:09:24.077 --> 01:09:25.556
Come back.


01:09:25.688 --> 01:09:26.863
- It's okay.
- I'm okay.


01:09:26.993 --> 01:09:30.301
Just breathe, breathe,
breathe, breathe, breathe.


01:09:30.431 --> 01:09:32.390
No, slow, slow.


01:09:32.520 --> 01:09:34.913
It's okay, it's okay.


01:09:35.045 --> 01:09:36.350
It'll be okay.


01:09:36.480 --> 01:09:38.003
You're gonna be okay.


01:09:39.658 --> 01:09:41.703
Bobby.


01:10:21.525 --> 01:10:23.572
- Teddy, come here.
- Get in, get in!


01:10:23.702 --> 01:10:25.617
God damn!


01:10:26.878 --> 01:10:28.445
Okay, come!


01:10:31.100 --> 01:10:32.275
- You're okay.
- Okay.


01:10:32.407 --> 01:10:34.278
- Yeah?
- I'm okay.


01:10:34.408 --> 01:10:35.801
I'm okay.


01:10:35.931 --> 01:10:37.194
Yeah.


01:10:42.634 --> 01:10:43.634
Is he?


01:10:45.854 --> 01:10:47.682
Yeah.


01:10:47.813 --> 01:10:49.685
He died just a few minutes ago.


01:10:52.948 --> 01:10:54.255
I'm sorry.


01:10:54.385 --> 01:10:55.385
It's not your fault.


01:10:55.472 --> 01:10:56.623
- I'm sorry.
- It's not your fault.


01:10:56.648 --> 01:10:58.432
I was just...


01:11:01.349 --> 01:11:02.610
Help me.


01:11:08.269 --> 01:11:09.356
Joe.


01:11:13.752 --> 01:11:15.057
Joe's still out there.


01:15:17.168 --> 01:15:18.867
Come on!


01:16:25.368 --> 01:16:26.587
Is that all of 'em?


01:16:27.935 --> 01:16:29.806
Yeah, I think so.


01:16:42.427 --> 01:16:44.256
How's your night going, Sheriff?


01:16:45.693 --> 01:16:47.345
I think it's gonna be okay.


01:16:49.521 --> 01:16:50.740
You all right, deputy?


01:16:53.351 --> 01:16:54.631
Yeah, I think I'll be all right.


01:16:56.006 --> 01:16:57.007
Good.


01:16:58.182 --> 01:16:59.967
What now, Joe?


01:17:00.097 --> 01:17:01.728
Well, I think we should
get the hell out of here


01:17:01.752 --> 01:17:03.667
and find the next
biggest town, do we all agree?


01:17:03.797 --> 01:17:04.667
Sounds like a plan.


01:17:04.798 --> 01:17:06.234
Yeah.


01:17:06.364 --> 01:17:08.628
We gotta find a car that
has a battery in it.


01:17:08.759 --> 01:17:10.412
Well, then let's go do that.


01:17:20.030 --> 01:17:22.163
So, how do you
like small towns, Sheriff?


01:17:24.862 --> 01:17:26.211
Think we could take the subway?


01:18:53.297 --> 01:18:55.474
Wow, what's going
on in the next town over?


01:18:55.604 --> 01:18:57.171
Seems to be a lot of
police action.


01:18:58.826 --> 01:19:01.610
No one cares about us
small town folks, Sheila.


01:19:01.742 --> 01:19:03.101
Hell, that's why I
moved to Ingram.


01:19:03.177 --> 01:19:04.658
Couldn't stand the
crowds and tourists


01:19:04.701 --> 01:19:06.354
and all that capitalism.


01:19:06.484 --> 01:19:07.484
Not for me.


01:19:09.662 --> 01:19:11.577
You're just such a sourpuss.


01:19:13.578 --> 01:19:16.320
That's what they say.


01:19:19.020 --> 01:19:21.631
Uh, what can I do for ya today?


01:19:21.761 --> 01:19:24.851
Well, you can tell me about
your quaint little town here.


01:22:59.935 --> 01:23:00.935
Thank you.


01:23:03.373 --> 01:23:04.984
Pretty interesting story, miss.


01:23:06.725 --> 01:23:07.944
Well, it's all true.


01:23:10.599 --> 01:23:11.774
Have you talked to Teddy?


01:23:13.253 --> 01:23:15.082
Or Joe?


01:23:15.212 --> 01:23:16.560
Sheriff Anderson? Yeah.


01:23:16.692 --> 01:23:17.735
Yeah, we have.


01:23:18.823 --> 01:23:21.565
Then you know everything.


01:23:21.697 --> 01:23:23.136
Well, it's a
rather farfetched story,


01:23:23.220 --> 01:23:25.527
certainly you can
understand that.


01:23:25.657 --> 01:23:26.876
But not untrue.


01:23:30.270 --> 01:23:31.551
Do you know where
the bodies are?


01:23:33.796 --> 01:23:34.796
The tree farm.


01:23:36.189 --> 01:23:37.930
Have you checked the tree farm?


01:23:39.715 --> 01:23:41.282
Yeah. Yeah, we did.


01:23:41.412 --> 01:23:43.239
Yeah, there was nothing there.


01:23:43.371 --> 01:23:44.894
Miss, to be honest,
there's no evidence


01:23:45.024 --> 01:23:47.287
that anyone was there other
than your own townsfolk.


01:23:47.417 --> 01:23:48.898
What?


01:23:49.029 --> 01:23:51.161
We know something happened,


01:23:51.292 --> 01:23:53.033
that you got missing
people, that's a fact.


01:23:54.643 --> 01:23:56.252
What about Georgia?


01:23:56.384 --> 01:23:57.904
She would never of left
her son's side,


01:23:57.993 --> 01:24:01.215
she had to been there
when you got there, right?


01:24:02.954 --> 01:24:04.869
Georgia's missing.


01:24:05.001 --> 01:24:06.001
We don't know where at.


01:24:07.655 --> 01:24:09.265
Dead.


01:24:09.396 --> 01:24:11.354
So what you're saying.


01:24:11.485 --> 01:24:13.792
Let the truth be told you
all have the same story,


01:24:13.922 --> 01:24:15.682
but there's no real
evidence of what happened


01:24:15.751 --> 01:24:17.404
other than a bunch of you
small town folk


01:24:17.534 --> 01:24:18.814
going a bit crazy coming up with


01:24:18.884 --> 01:24:21.016
a very bizarre
account of events.


01:24:21.148 --> 01:24:22.453
So, help me here.


01:24:22.583 --> 01:24:24.412
What is it you're
not telling us?


01:24:24.542 --> 01:24:28.024
It doesn't matter what I
tell you, you won't believe


01:24:28.154 --> 01:24:29.675
what we saw until you
see for yourself.

